We have it happen on a semi-regular basis over here.  The most extreme,
though, was a senate race a couple of years ago.  The incumbent was
headed to defeat by the challentger when he died with extraordinarily
good timing--too late to change the candidates, so if he was elected,
the governor would get to appoint someone to serve until the next
election.  

The governor (same party) announced that he'd appoint the widow if he
won, and the sympathy vote put her over the top.  As it turns out, this
actually made a difference in control of the senate.  If memory serves,
she lost in the special election twoyears later.

